This is 4va, the 4th dimensional graphics viewer for X-Windows.
Please see the man page "doc/4va.1" for details (to format it, use
the command "nroff -man doc/4va.1 | ul").

Build with "meson setup build && meson compile -C build". Sample
object files are in data/, e.g. "build/4va data/hcube.4vd".

Recommended: on a modern display, run

  build/4va -nd -rpresent -aa -control data

to stay in the foreground, show frames in sync with the display, draw
anti-aliased lines, and browse the objects in data/ from the window
(left/right: object, up/down: line color, q: quit). These aren't the
defaults, which stay close to the original behavior; -rpresent and -aa
fall back with a warning if unsupported.

Please send any questions or bugs to mdw1@crux2.cit.cornell.edu.

Share and Enjoy!
Matt Welsh
